      "patch": "@@ -24,8 +24,9 @@\n #     install platform's tree; it installs the artefact its own composition rendered from\n #     platform's and nist's signed parents (composed/HEADER.yaml records those parent SHAs, and\n #     fact 3 of the sample checks the live platform and nist pins against them).\n-#   * apps and composed delivery use the same genuine v4.0.0 Source A release.\n-#     Its complete policy window and signature gates move with the inventory binding.\n+#   * composed delivery uses genuine v4.0.1 Composition B, whose signed tree binds\n+#     apps and native inventory to Source A v4.0.0. Its complete window is5.0.0,6.0.0,7.0.0.\n+#     Apps and inventory remain A; this reviewed pointer moves only composed delivery to B.\n #   * there is no `spec.verify` here. Flux's GitRepository.spec.verify speaks OpenPGP, and one\n #     signature -- the gitsign tag -- is the only one this estate has (ADR-0023, D3). Verification\n #     at the source boundary is the identity-pinned gitsign-verifying controller of ticket 41,\n@@ -69,9 +70,9 @@ spec:\n   interval: 1m\n   url: https://github.com/policy-as-versioned-driftwood/driftwood\n   ref:\n-    tag: v4.0.0\n-    commit: 1cd446f62a531c0aeee7e50c0a59a11ac5d00d67\n-    # The resolved SHA of the genuine signed v4.0.0 Source A release.\n+    tag: v4.0.1\n+    commit: 872d5c7f44801b496731b11cd40881f304f8a09a\n+    # The resolved SHA of the genuine signed v4.0.1 Composition B release.\n     # Belt-and-braces immutability, ADR-0001.\n ---\n apiVersion: fluxcd.controlplane.io/v1"
